  <prompt>
    Extend the canonical communication architecture doc **`docs/architecture/communication-intelligence-architecture.md`** (the R4/R1 substrate that R1 task 081 already extended) to describe the R2 **read / query / organize layer** as-built. Use the `docs-architecture` skill.

    Prefer EXTENDING this canonical doc (and/or `communication-service-architecture.md` if the read/query narrative needs it) rather than authoring a new standalone doc (§11 — the communication platform is ONE platform; R2 is its read/organize layer, not a new subsystem). Add, grounded in the shipped code:

    - **The Workspace read endpoints** — `GET /api/communications/by-regarding/{entityType}/{id}` (FR-01/010) + the filtered `GET /api/communications?thread=&regarding=&channel=&from=&to=&participant=` (FR-02/011/051); how they EXTEND `CommunicationThreadReadService` + `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` + `ICommunicationAccessFilter` (the blessed R1 impersonation read path); the entity-set-agnostic behavior across all 11 regarding families; the impersonation + 2-rule (privacy + internal-only) access filter; **NO membership-union on reads** (retired 2026-07-16), **no new access mechanism**.
    - **The participant index** — the `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction (message grain; `sprk_communication` parent + two typed nullable person lookups `sprk_systemuser`/`sprk_contact` [exactly one set] + role {From/To/Cc/Bcc} + `sprk_addresstext` + `sprk_isresolved`); populated at capture/send reusing `ParticipantCorrelationRung`; unresolved external addresses written as rows; how it powers the `participant=` facet; the ADR-034 path-C rationale (2 typed lookups honor the tuple *intent*). Cross-reference the participant-junction ADR (task 004).
    - **The auto-threading policy** — the 3-tier `IThreadResolver` (subject/conversation → per-record default → per-user master) + the `default-thread` marker; the marker-gated `BuildTopic` naming re-derive; the thread typed-regarding lookups + Lookup discriminator + RegardingResolver placement (FR-06/07/09).
    - **Surface 1 — the regarding-mode Timeline** (FR-03/020) — the `CommunicationTimeline` regarding mode (threads-as-collapsible-groups → interleaved email+chat), the form-bound PCF on all 11 forms, the count-only VisualHost card (T-1 boundary: content flows only through the BFF `internal-only` filter, never VisualHost client-fetch).
    - **Surface 3 — the workspace widget** (FR-12) — the `communications-list` Pattern D upgrade in `@spaarke/communication-components`, dual-deploy (LegalWorkspace + SpaarkeAi), type-string preserved.

    Cross-reference the relevant ADRs (024 regarding, 034 membership/participant, 028 auth/impersonation, 032 kill-switch, 046 channel / no second regarding mechanism, 038 testing) + the task-004 participant ADR. Keep it a design/rationale doc (WHY + structure) with code entry-point pointers — no implementation dumps.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke architecture writer authoritative on the Communication subsystem. Uses the `docs-architecture` skill and follows repo architecture-doc conventions (decisions + rationale + code entry-point pointers). Extends the canonical R4/R1 communication doc rather than forking a new one.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `docs/architecture/communication-intelligence-architecture.md` (and `communication-service-architecture.md` if needed) accurately describe the R2 as-built read/organize layer — Workspace read endpoints, participant index, auto-threading policy + thread regarding/naming, the regarding-mode Timeline (Surface 1), and the workspace widget (Surface 3) — cross-referencing the relevant ADRs + the task-004 participant ADR. The doc matches shipped code and is extended (not forked) from the canonical substrate.
  </goal>

  <context>
